.TH DHCPRELAYD 8 "November 2026" "dhcprelayd" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dhcprelayd \- DHCP relay agent with option 82 support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhcprelayd
.RB [ \-dhv ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dhcprelayd
is a DHCP and BOOTP relay agent.  It picks up requests that clients
broadcast on a local network and relays them as unicast to one or more
DHCP servers on another network.  It relays the replies back to the
clients.
.PP
The relay agent can run on a routed interface, but it is mainly made for
a switch: a VLAN filtering bridge where each bridge port connects to one
client.  For each request it
.IP \(bu 3
sets the gateway address,
.IR giaddr ,
to its address on the client network, the server uses it to select the
subnet and sends its reply to it,
.IP \(bu
adds the relay agent information option, option 82 from RFC 3046, with
the
.I circuit-id
of the port the request came in on and the
.I remote-id
of the relay agent, if enabled,
.IP \(bu
sends the request to all servers configured for the interface.
.PP
Replies are relayed only from the servers of the interface, others are
dropped.  For each reply it removes option 82, adds an FDB entry for the client on
the port the request came in on, and an ARP entry for the offered
address, and sends the reply to the client.  The FDB entry is for switch
cores that do not learn from frames trapped to the CPU.
.PP
Requests already relayed by another relay agent, with
.I giaddr
set, are forwarded unchanged.  Requests with one of the relay agent's
own gateway addresses in
.I giaddr
are dropped.
.PP
On a bridge,
.B dhcprelayd
installs
.BR nft (8)
rules that drop DHCP requests from the configured bridge ports, so the
bridge does not flood them to the other ports.  The rules are in the
chains
.B dhcpr-input
and
.B dhcpr-forward
of the
.B bridge filter
table, and are removed when the relay agent stops.
.PP
The relay agent binds UDP port 67 only on its gateway addresses, so a
DHCP server can run on the same system.  The server must allow a second
socket on port 67, with
.B \-\-bind\-dynamic
or
.B \-\-bind\-interfaces
for
.BR dnsmasq (8),
and the relay agent reaches it at 127.0.0.1, see
.BR dhcprelayd.conf (5).
.PP
The configuration file is described in
.BR dhcprelayd.conf (5).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read the configuration from
.IR file ,
default
.IR /etc/dhcprelayd.conf .
.TP
.B \-d
Log all levels to stdout instead of syslog, for debugging.
.TP
.B \-v
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Read the configuration file again.  If the new file is invalid, the
error is logged and the relay agent keeps running with the old
configuration.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT ", " SIGQUIT
Remove the nftables rules and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dhcprelayd.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dhcprelayd
exits 0 when stopped by a signal, and 1 when the configuration file is
missing or invalid at startup, or when it fails to set up its sockets.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcprelayd.conf (5),
.BR nft (8),
.BR dnsmasq (8)
.PP
RFC 3046, DHCP Relay Agent Information Option.
.br
RFC 5107, DHCP Server Identifier Override Suboption.
